Flow:
Parse JSON -> Apply to each parsed row

Detail

Power Apps (send only the columns the flow needs)
  Set(payloadJson, JSON(ShowColumns(colChecklist, Title, IsComplete, SortOrder), JSONFormat.Compact));
  Set(flowResult, RunFlow.Run(selectedRequest.ID, payloadJson));
  If(flowResult.success = "true", Notify("Saved", NotificationType.Success), Notify(flowResult.message, NotificationType.Error))

Flow
  Trigger: Power Apps (V2)
    Inputs: RequestId (Number), Payload (Text)

  Parse JSON
    Content : @{triggerBody()?['text']}        (the Payload input)
    Schema  :
    {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "Title":      { "type": "string" },
          "IsComplete": { "type": "boolean" },
          "SortOrder":  { "type": ["number", "null"] }
        },
        "required": ["Title"]
      }
    }

  Apply to each: @{body('Parse_JSON')}
    Create item (Checklist Items)
      Title      : @{items('Apply_to_each')?['Title']}
      IsComplete : @{items('Apply_to_each')?['IsComplete']}
      SortOrder  : @{items('Apply_to_each')?['SortOrder']}
      RequestId  : @{triggerBody()?['number']}

  Respond to a Power App or flow
    success (Text) : true          message (Text) : @{length(body('Parse_JSON'))} rows saved

Without Parse JSON
  Apply to each over  json(triggerBody()?['text'])  and read values with items('Apply_to_each')?['Title'].
  You lose the dynamic content picker but avoid schema failures.

