Flow outline:
When item status is Approved -> Create Planner task -> Update SharePoint item with Planner task ID and link

Flow detail

Trigger: When an item is created or modified
  Trigger conditions:
    @equals(triggerBody()?['Status']?['Value'], 'Approved')
    @empty(triggerBody()?['PlannerTaskId'])

Create a task (Planner)
  Group Id          : the Microsoft 365 group that owns the plan
  Plan Id           : the plan
  Title             : @{triggerBody()?['Title']}
  Bucket Id         : the bucket for new work
  Start Date Time   : @{utcNow()}
  Due Date Time     : @{triggerBody()?['DueDate']}
  Assigned User Ids : @{triggerBody()?['AssignedTo']?['Email']}        (several: separate with semicolons)

Update task details (Planner)
  Task Id     : @{outputs('Create_a_task')?['body/id']}
  Description : @{triggerBody()?['Description']}
  References  : Resource link @{triggerBody()?['{Link}']}, Alias "SharePoint request"
  Checklist   : add an item per step if needed

Update item (SharePoint)
  PlannerTaskId   : @{outputs('Create_a_task')?['body/id']}
  PlannerTaskLink : https://planner.cloud.microsoft/webui/v1/plan/<plan-id>/view/board/task/@{outputs('Create_a_task')?['body/id']}

Sync completion back to SharePoint (second flow)
  Trigger   : When a task is completed (Planner), same group and plan
  Get items : Filter Query  PlannerTaskId eq '@{triggerOutputs()?['body/id']}'   Top Count 1
  Update item: Status = Completed, CompletedOn = @{utcNow()}

Columns needed
  PlannerTaskId (single line of text, indexed), PlannerTaskLink (hyperlink or text)

Limits to know
  The connector creates basic plan tasks. The assignee must be a member of the plan's group.
  Labels are set with the Update a task action. Priority uses numbers: 1 urgent, 3 important, 5 medium, 9 low.

